('The fossil fuel industry spent $137 million lobbying to protect $17-35 billion of subsidies, a 12,300% return; tax expenditures cost $1.8 trillion, more than Social Security or defense.','12,300% return','K02: 17e9/137e6 = 124x, about 12,309% (reproduces at the low end). The subsidy range is contested by definition. Total tax expenditures of ~$1.8-1.9T exceed Social Security outlays, but summing them is methodologically disputed ('+R+').',[]),
('Total tax burden has stayed near 31% since 1980; the composition shifted from corporations to payroll taxes.','Total burden has stayed near 31% since 1980','The federal+state+local burden is roughly stable ('+R+'). The video\'s own conclusion that the middle class "isn\'t being taxed more overall" contradicts its title.',[]),
